    <string name="waiting_title">Waiting for a privilege path</string>
    <string name="waiting_body">Broadcast needs a supported privilege path: Shizuku on many Samsung phones, or root. See Compatibility for details.</string>
    <string name="waiting_retry">Retry</string>
    <string name="waiting_open_compatibility">Compatibility</string>
    <string name="nav_compatibility">Compatibility</string>
    <string name="compatibility_title">Compatibility</string>
    <string name="compatibility_intro">Mirax can only advertise a Miracast sink when something on the phone may call setWfdInfo (CONFIGURE_WIFI_DISPLAY). That is not a normal install permission.</string>
    <string name="compatibility_supported_title">Supported</string>
    <string name="compatibility_supported_body">• Samsung (many models): install Shizuku, authorize Mirax, then Retry.\n• Rooted: grant root when prompted; Mirax starts the sink helper as UID 0.</string>
    <string name="compatibility_unsupported_title">Not supported</string>
    <string name="compatibility_unsupported_body">Stock OEM phones that give CONFIGURE_WIFI_DISPLAY neither to shell nor to a sideloaded app, and that are not rooted, cannot broadcast. Opening Shizuku alone is not enough if the OEM denied the permission to UID 2000.</string>
    <string name="compatibility_denied_banner">Broadcast could not start: the privilege path did not reach Wi‑Fi Direct listening. This phone may be unsupported.</string>
